  Primeiro, devemos calcular as distribuições marginais de \(X\) e
  \(Y\).

  \begin{longtable}[]{@{}ccccccccc@{}}
  \toprule\noalign{}
  \(Y\setminus X\) & \(2\) & \(3\) & \(4\) & \(\mathbb{P}(Y=y)\) & & &
  & \\
  \midrule\noalign{}
  \endhead
  \bottomrule\noalign{}
  \endlastfoot
  \(2\) & 0.064 & 0.155 & 0.112 & 0.331 & & & & \\
  \(3\) & 0.2 & 0.05 & 0.053 & 0.303 & & & & \\
  \(4\) & 0.033 & 0.098 & 0.044 & 0.175 & & & & \\
  \(5\) & 0.007 & 0.12 & 0.064 & 0.191 & & & & \\
  \(\mathbb{P}(X=x)\) & 0.304 & 0.423 & 0.273 & 1 & & & & \\
  \end{longtable}

  Daí, segue que \[\mathbb{P}(X \geq 3|Y = 4) = 
  \frac{\mathbb{P}(X \geq 3, Y = 4)}{P(Y = 4)}=
  \frac{\sum_{x=3}^{4} p(x,4)}{\mathbb{P}(Y=4)} =
  \frac{0.142}{0.175} = 0.811.\]

